          "_name": "content1",
          "_customHTML": "<section class=\"mbr-section article content1\">\n    \n    <mbr-parameters>\n    <!-- Block parameters controls (Blue \"Gear\" panel) -->\n        <input type=\"range\" inline title=\"Top\" name=\"paddingTop\" min=\"0\" max=\"8\" step=\"1\" value=\"4\">\n        <input type=\"range\" inline title=\"Bottom\" name=\"paddingBottom\" min=\"0\" max=\"8\" step=\"1\" value=\"4\">\n        <input type=\"color\" title=\"Background Color\" name=\"bgColor\" value=\"#ffffff\">\n    <!-- End block parameters -->\n    </mbr-parameters> \n\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <div class=\"media-container-row\">\n            <div class=\"mbr-text col-12 col-md-8 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-7\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" data-multiline mbr-article>The design of the UBDA infrastructure is shown in Figure 3. The Service Layer is a&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">common management layer providing the interface of accessing and using the underlying&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">big data facility. It allows the users to login to the UBDA system to manage their profile,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">access to the allocated resources, install and configure their applications, and manage&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">their jobs though the job scheduler.</span><div><br></div><div>The Application Layer provides modeling and programming support for individual&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">researchers to develop application of different areas and is composed of domain-specific&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">models, languages and algorithms, some of which are represented as software tools and&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">libraries. Application Layer contains common tools e.g. C/C++ complier, Fortran, and R&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">script (please see Table 3 of Appendix A for a list of software). Researchers also can&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">install their own software to support their research.</span></div><div><br></div><div>The big data Computing Cluster Layer is a key component of the UBDA infrastructure.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">It consists of a pool of various types of hardware server nodes, e.g. General CPU node,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">MIC node and GPU node, which can be configured to form the required clusters for&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">different kinds of big data analytics projects, supporting both data intensive and&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">computation intensive processing tasks. The total initial capacity is planed to be able to&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">support around 123 Tflops.</span></div><div><br></div><div>The Network Layer contains two types of networks (Infiniband and Ethernet). The i<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">nfiniband is a high speed 56 G (FDR) network, which is mainly for internal&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">interconnection of computing nodes with low latency and non-blocking data transfer to&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">support big data analysis. The Ethernet network is mainly for external connection to the&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">campus network and public internet.</span></div><div><br></div><div>The storage layer consists of 400TB storage system with parallel file systems to allow&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">research to storage and process their research data in a reliable environment.</span></div></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
